{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>יזה</b> Two: יזה and the other כן יזה גוים רבים, in the passage הנה ישכיל עבדי, which speaks of the messiah, that the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to restore the two families. When King Messiah comes, the priestly family (and the house of David) too will return to their service:" "<b> ולפני הכפורת יזה ז\"פ</b> Why one sprinkle above and seven below? For it suffices for those below to be one of seven of those above. So too David said: seven — הללו את ה' מן השמים, and one — הללו את ה' מן הארץ. And so Moses did not mention the Name in האזינו until after 21 words, saying: it suffices that I be one of seven of the angels who mention the Name after three words. 16 sprinklings upon the kapporet, corresponding to 16 covenants struck at Sinai. 16 upon the parokhet, corresponding to 16 in the Tent of Meeting. 16 upon the golden altar, with the remnants of blood on the outer altar, corresponding to 16 in the plains of Moab — and that is what is written: דם הברית. And 5 immersions, corresponding to 5 services where he changes from outside to inside and from inside to outside, and corresponding to 5 prayers, and they correspond to the 5 times מלך הכבוד in the psalm לה' הארץ ומלואה. And they come to atone for the soul that has 5 names. And 10 kiddushin, corresponding to 10 times the Name is mentioned on that day. And in the passage, 10 times the Name until תטהרו. And 24 atonements are written in the matter of Yom HaKippurim — in ובאתה תצוה and בהר סיני and here, and in אמור אל הכהנים, and in פנחס לכפר — corresponding to 24 transgressions in Ezekiel in the passage הודע את ירושלים, and 24 forbidden relations written in this order."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The two cited occurrences of יזה are Leviticus 16:14 and Isaiah 52:15 (כן יזה גוים רבים). The passage הנה ישכיל עבדי is Isaiah 52:13ff."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:42.950976759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}